-- title:
--   Finiteness of the répartition space H¹(D)
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $F$ be fields with $F$ a $K$-algebra satisfying `IsCurveOver K F`, i.e. every nonzero $f \in F$ has an associated divisor of degree $0$ whose value at each place $v$ is $\operatorname{ord}_v f$, every place of $F/K$ has residue field finite over $K$, and $\Omega_{F/K}$ is free of rank one over $F$. Assume the set of places `Place K F` (valuation subrings of $F$ containing the image of $K$, proper and principal ideal rings) is nonempty, and that $L(0)$, the space of $f \in F$ with $v(f) \le 1$ at every place, is finite-dimensional over $K$. Let $\gamma \in \mathbb{Z}$ and let $D_0$ be a divisor (a finitely supported function from places to $\mathbb{Z}$) such that `RiemannGenusReachedAt γ D₀` holds: $L(D_0)$ is finite-dimensional, $\deg D_0 - \ell(D_0) = \gamma - 1$, and $\deg D - \ell(D) \le \gamma - 1$ for every divisor $D$. Then for every divisor $D$ the quotient $H^1(D)$ of the algebra of répartitions (the $F$-subalgebra of $\prod_v F$ generated by the families $\alpha$ with $v(\alpha_v) \le 1$ for all but finitely many $v$) by the sum of the submodule of répartitions with $v(\alpha_v) \le \exp(D v)$ for all $v$ and the image of $F$ under the diagonal embedding is a finite-dimensional $K$-vector space.
--
--   This is the finiteness half of the Riemann–Roch theorem, in the répartition (Čech) formulation: the first cohomology of a divisor on a one-variable function field is finite-dimensional over the base field. It is used in the proof of the répartition form of Riemann–Roch, [`AlgebraicCurve.cechRiemannRoch_of_genusReached`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.cechRiemannRoch_of_genusReached).
